\
But it has this inevitable disadvantage, so far as \
others are concerned that ic is something which it is \
quite impossible for him to pass on. And this be- \
comes felt a real difficulty when, a- occasionally hap- \
pens, any student of Krishnamurti\'92s teachings is ask- \
ed by friends to give them some idea of the main out- \
line of his message and to single out its fundamental \
