Wc cannot hold out against those who have betray- \
ed the truth they have heard by wanting to teach it to \
others. They did not intend to turn false the words \
of wisdom. But how could they, imperfect as they \
\\vere. transmit without corrupting the message of per- \
fection? Even if true to the letter of what they he^, \
